{"conversation_id":"ab5d9eed-50ac-41ff-a108-7216b070e626","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-10 22:16:02 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-11 05:16:02 ICT\n\nReviewed `778747ce..db2434dd` (and net branch diff `8cd9fc92..db2434dd`) statically against the four findings in [1794341300000-reviewer-r3-exception-clojure.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/exception-track/1794341300000-reviewer-r3-exception-clojure.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log). All line references in [clojure.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc) and [clojure_test.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_test.clj) below are at `db2434dd`. No files were edited.\n\n---\n\n### Per-Finding Verdicts\n\n1. **P1-1 (retained tokens are source-readable and transferable / R5): CONFIRMED FIXED** ([clojure.cljc:923-958](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L923-L958), [clojure_test.clj:1592-1641](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_test.clj#L1592-L1641)).\n   - Provenance no longer lives in a source-readable map key (`:dsg__condition`). Instead, `dsg__condition_wrapper` ([clojure.cljc:931-935](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L931-L935)) allocates a cell holding `[visible condition witness]`, where `witness` is a host-typed [`Closure`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/values.cljc#L43-L76) minted by `dsg__condition_witness` ([clojure.cljc:923-928](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L923-L928)) closing over `dsg__visible`, `dsg__condition`, `dsg__call_token`, and `dsg__equal`.\n   - `dsg__condition_retained` ([clojure.cljc:938-958](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L938-L958)) re-derives `(dsg__condition_witness dsg__visible dsg__condition)` from the cell's first two slots and compares it with `dsg__proof` via `dsg__equal` ([`data/content=`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc#L484-L493)). Neither keyword lookup nor cell inspection yields a token that can authenticate a different `[visible condition]` pair (see Ruling on Invariant 1 below).\n\n2. **P1-2 (ordinary caught exceptions expose the wrapper instead of the original exception): STILL BROKEN (P1)** ([clojure.cljc:961-993](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L961-L993), [clojure.cljc:1218-1222](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1218-L1222), [clojure.cljc:1617-1626](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1617-L1626)).\n   - **What `db2434dd` fixed:** [`rewrite-ex-info`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L977-L1004) lowers `(ex-message x)`, `(.getMessage x)`, and `(ex-data x)` to `dsg__ex_message` / `dsg__ex_data` ([clojure.cljc:961-974](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L961-L974)), which decode `dsg__condition_retained` and read `:yin.k/message` / `:yin.k/data` from slot 0 (`dsg__visible`).\n   - **What remains broken (P1):**\n     1. **Catch binder still receives the wrapper `:cell-ref`, breaking payload identity (`=`) and regressing Round 0's green `[:clojure :python :round-trip]` contract row:**\n        At [clojure.cljc:1618-1626](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1618-L1626), `condition-\u003eoutcome` wraps every `:yang.call/thrown` payload in `(dsg__condition_wrapper (:yang.call/value condition) condition)`, which allocates a **new `:cell-ref`** `{:type :cell-ref, :id :cell-k, :seal \"...\"}`. At [clojure.cljc:1220](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1220), `try` binds the catch variable `e` directly to `(data/nth outcome 1)` — that wrapper `:cell-ref`, **not** `dsg__visible`.\n        In Round 0's cross-language contract suite ([exception_legs.clj:44](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/call/exception_legs.clj#L44)), Clojure's `home` is:\n        ```clojure\n        (defn home [f done] (try (f) false (catch Exception e (and (= e original) (done)))))\n        ```\n        where `original` is `(def original (cell/new :original))` ([exception_contract.clj:73](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/call/exception_contract.clj#L73)). When `(f)` (`probe_round_trip` in Python) re-raises `{:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown, :yang.call/value original}` back to `home`, `condition-\u003eoutcome` wraps `original` (`:cell-0`) in a new wrapper cell (`:cell-k`). In `home`'s catch handler, `(= e original)` compares `:cell-k` against `:cell-0` via primitive `=` and evaluates to **`false`**.\n        Consequently, `[:clojure :python :round-trip]` — which was **`:green`** on `:semantic`, `:stack`, and `:register` on `master` ([exception_r0_results.edn:75, 170](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/call/exception_r0_results.edn#L170)) — **regresses to `:red`** (`{:returned true, :value false}`), violating [Ruling v2 §R2(1)](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/exception-track/1794960000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity-v2.md#L27-L31) (*\"a payload valid in the receiving runtime keeps its ordinary catching and identity behavior — delivered UNCHANGED\"*) and [§8.10.7](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.antlr.md#L3868-L3882) (*\"Crossing back into a runtime recognizing the original exception restores its original type and identity\"*).\n     2. **Ordinary catch behavior still depends on routing for every operation on `e` except `ex-message`/`.getMessage`/`ex-data`:**\n        - `(let [orig (ex-info \"boom\" {:x 1}) f (fn [] (throw orig))] (try (f) (catch Exception e (= e orig))))` yields **`false`** across a dynamic call vs **`true`** across an intra-unit call.\n        - 3-argument `(ex-info \"boom\" {:x 1} :cause)` lowers to `{:yin.k/message \"boom\", :yin.k/data {:x 1}, :yin.k/cause :cause}` ([clojure.cljc:996-999](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L996-L999)); across a dynamic call, `(:yin.k/cause e)`, `(:yin.k/message e)`, `(get e :yin.k/data)`, custom map keys `(:code e)`, and scalar/collection predicates on `e` all inspect the `:cell-ref` wrapper map (`{:type :cell-ref, :id ..., :seal ...}`) and yield `nil` / `false`. Likewise, `(:yang.call/reason e)` on a caught protocol condition yields `nil`.\n     3. **Nested wrapper breaks `ex-message` / `ex-data` (Invariant 3):**\n        If a caught wrapper `e` is returned as a value (e.g., `(defn capture [f] (try (f) (catch Exception e e)))`, matching `retain` at [exception_contract.clj:78](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/call/exception_contract.clj#L78)) and then thrown as the payload of a fresh `:yang.call/thrown` condition across a dynamic call, `condition-\u003eoutcome` ([clojure.cljc:1623-1625](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1623-L1625)) sets the outer wrapper's `dsg__visible` to the inner wrapper `:cell-ref`. Because `dsg__ex_message` and `dsg__ex_data` ([clojure.cljc:966, 974](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L966)) decode only one wrapper layer, `(ex-message e2)` and `(ex-data e2)` return `[nil nil]`.\n\n3. **P1-3 (retention deletes an original `:dsg__condition` field): CONFIRMED FIXED** ([clojure.cljc:931-958](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L931-L958), [clojure.cljc:1390-1400](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1390-L1400), [clojure.cljc:2543-2551](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2543-L2551), [clojure_test.clj:1644-1673](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_test.clj#L1644-L1673)).\n   - The original condition map is stored at index 1 of the wrapper cell untouched (no `dsg__assoc` on reception, no `data/dissoc` at `call-entry` or `strip-top-outcome`). Both immediate (`receive`) and saved (`retain` + `later`) rethrows preserve `:dsg__condition :ordinary-evidence` byte-for-byte.\n\n4. **P2-4 (two updated value-path assertions do not pin the outer contract): CONFIRMED FIXED** ([clojure_test.clj:2734-2766](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_test.clj#L2734-L2766)).\n   - Both the projected raw-closure assertion ([clojure_test.clj:2734-2742](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_test.clj#L2734-L2742)) and the `tail-refusal` assertion ([clojure_test.clj:2751-2766](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_test.clj#L2751-L2766)) now pin `:yin.k/error`, outer `:yang.call/thrown` reason, inner `:yang.call/not-callable` reason, and `:yang.call/callee` evidence.\n\n---\n\n### Explicit Rulings on the Four Invariants\n\n1. **Invariant 1 — Cell forgery (`cell/authentic?` + witness re-derivation): HOLDS (P1-1 is genuinely closed, with one minorP3 shape-guard note).**\n   - **Can guest code mint an authentic cell or copy/mutate cell contents?** **Yes.** In `yang.clojure`, `cell/new`, `cell/get`, and `cell/set!` are admitted host-module exports ([`native-name?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L818-L826)). `(cell/new v)` ([engine.cljc:2773-2778](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2773-L2778)) issues a task-sealed `:cell-ref` via [`issue-ref`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L317-L329) that satisfies [`authentic-ref?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L332-L346) (`(cell/authentic? c) =\u003e true`). Guest code can also read `[visible condition witness]` from a caught wrapper `e` via `(cell/get e)` and copy or overwrite it via `cell/new` / `cell/set!`.\n   - **Why forgery and witness transplant still fail:** `cell/authentic?` at [clojure.cljc:941](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L941) is only a non-fatal guard so `(cell/get dsg__candidate)` does not fail closed in [`check-ref!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L355-L373). Content authentication rests on [`dsg__condition_witness`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L923-L928) and `dsg__equal` ([`data-content=`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc#L484-L493)):\n     - `dsg__condition_witness` returns a kernel-minted [`yin.vm.values/Closure`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/values.cljc#L43-L76). [`values/closure?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/values.cljc#L151-L155) is an `instance? Closure` check, so no guest map carrying `:type :closure` satisfies [`data/callable?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc#L456-L460).\n     - On `Closure` instances, [`data-content=`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc#L491-L492) delegates to host `=`, which compares `owner` and kernel `payload` ([values.cljc:46-69](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/values.cljc#L46-L69)) — i.e., the inner lambda's compiled code/entry AND its captured lexical environment `{dsg__visible, dsg__condition, dsg__call_token, dsg__equal}`.\n     - Guest source cannot name `dsg__condition_witness`, `dsg__condition_wrapper`, or `dsg__call_token` ([`check-program-symbols!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2482-L2506)), so no guest-authored `(fn [q] ...)` can have the same `payload`.\n     - If guest code extracts `witness` via `(nth (cell/get e) 2)` and places `[forged-visible forged-condition witness]` into a new cell or via `cell/set!`, `(dsg__condition_witness forged-visible forged-condition)` at [clojure.cljc:950-951](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L950-L951) mints a `Closure` whose captured environment binds `dsg__visible = forged-visible` and `dsg__condition = forged-condition`, which is unequal (`=`) to `witness`'s captured `{dsg__visible orig-visible, dsg__condition orig-condition}` whenever either slot differs.\n     - Copying the unchanged triple `(cell/new (cell/get e))` into a new cell only reproduces the exact `[orig-visible orig-condition]` that `(throw e)` was already authorized to forward.\n   - *P3 note:* Unlike [`cell-ref-shaped-node`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1479-L1503) and [`dsg__admitted?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2662-L2687), `condition-retained-form` ([clojure.cljc:940-941](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L940-L941)) does not check `(dsg__equal (data/count dsg__candidate) 3)` before `(cell/authentic? dsg__candidate)`, and [`engine/authentic-ref?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L341-L346) ignores extra keys on a `:cell-ref` map. This does not allow forging a condition (`(assoc e :yang.call/reason :forged)` still decodes to `e`'s original `condition`, as tested in `test-exception-r3-modified-condition-refuses` at [clojure_test.clj:1621-1641](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_test.clj#L1621-L1641)).\n\n2. **Invariant 2 — No guest-applied callable on the error path: HOLDS.**\n   - `dsg__condition_retained` ([clojure.cljc:938-958](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L938-L958)), `dsg__ex_message` ([clojure.cljc:961-966](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L961-L966)), `dsg__ex_data` ([clojure.cljc:969-974](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L969-L974)), `call-entry` ([clojure.cljc:1390-1400](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1390-L1400)), and `strip-top-outcome` ([clojure.cljc:2543-2551](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2543-L2551)) never invoke `dsg__proof` or any guest value; they call only `data/*`, `cell/authentic?`, `cell/get`, `conj`, and compiler-bound `dsg__*` closures.\n\n3. **Invariant 3 — Visible/retained divergence: FAILS (P1 — see P1-2 above).**\n   - Slot 0 (`dsg__visible`) and what the guest actually observes on the caught binding `e` diverge for every operation except `(ex-message e)`, `(.getMessage e)`, and `(ex-data e)`, because `try` ([clojure.cljc:1220](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1220)) binds `e` to the wrapper `:cell-ref` while `=` and map lookups (`get`, keyword calls) do not unwrap `dsg__visible`.\n   - Additionally, `dsg__condition_wrapper` ([clojure.cljc:931-935](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L931-L935)) does not unwrap `dsg__visible` when `dsg__visible` is itself already a wrapper cell (e.g. a caught wrapper returned as a value and rethrown across another boundary as a `:yang.call/thrown` payload), causing single-layer `dsg__ex_message`/`dsg__ex_data` to read `:yin.k/message`/`:yin.k/data` off the inner `:cell-ref` and return `nil`.\n\n4. **Invariant 4 — Test integrity \u0026 non-semantic churn: HOLDS for existing tests in `clojure_test.clj`, but `[:clojure :python :round-trip]` in the deferred contract suite regresses.**\n   - Within `778747ce..db2434dd`, no existing expectation in [clojure_test.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_test.clj) was weakened or moved; the two P2-4 assertions were strengthened and four new regression `deftest`s were added. Across `8cd9fc92..db2434dd`, the remaining non-semantic diff is purely formatter reflowing of `defn` forms.\n\n---\n\n### Minimal Disposition to Close P1-2 \u0026 Invariant 3\n\n1. **Unwrap `dsg__visible` in `dsg__condition_wrapper` ([clojure.cljc:931-935](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L931-L935)) so wrapper `visible` slots never nest:**\n   Bind a small helper (e.g. `dsg__visible_of`):\n   ```clojure\n   (fn [dsg__value]\n     (let [dsg__decoded (dsg__condition_retained dsg__value)]\n       (if (dsg__equal dsg__decoded nil)\n         dsg__value\n         (data/nth dsg__decoded 0))))\n   ```\n   and normalize `dsg__visible` through `(dsg__visible_of dsg__visible)` inside `condition-wrapper-form` before constructing the cell and witness.\n2. **Route guest `=` and guest `get` / keyword lookups through `dsg__visible_of` (or unwrap 2-key `:yang.call/thrown` payloads at `catch` when not rethrown):**\n   - Routing guest `=` (both operands via `dsg__visible_of`) and guest `get` / keyword lookups ([clojure.cljc:1794-1800](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1794-L1800), map operand via `dsg__visible_of`) ensures that:\n     - `(= e original)` in `home` ([exception_legs.clj:44](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/call/exception_legs.clj#L44)) and `(= e orig)` on caught `ex-info`/values evaluate to `true` (keeping `[:clojure :python :round-trip]` green);\n     - `(:yin.k/cause e)`, `(:yin.k/message e)`, `(get e :yin.k/data)`, custom map keys `(:code e)`, and `(:yang.call/reason e)` on caught protocol conditions all read `dsg__visible` transparently while `(:dsg__condition e)` on a marker-free protocol condition still returns `nil`;\n     - `e` itself remains the authenticated wrapper cell so `(throw e)` and `(cell/set! saved e)` + `(throw (cell/get saved))` continue to forward `dsg__condition` unchanged through `call-entry` and `strip-top-outcome`.\n   - Add assertions in `test-exception-r3-ordinary-call-catch-keeps-payload-behavior` ([clojure_test.clj:1565](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_test.clj#L1565)) covering `(= e orig)` (including when `orig` is a `(cell/new :original)` as in `exception_legs.clj:44`) and `(:yin.k/cause e)` / keyword lookup across a dynamic call.\n\n**CHANGES STILL REQUIRED**\n","duration_seconds":1271.691558,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":489019,"output_tokens":83745,"thinking_tokens":74283,"cache_read_tokens":4888796,"total_tokens":572764}}
